    {
      "FullInfo": "Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.PICore.PICore.PIPOMModel.DataModel.CharacteristicSpecification",
      "ReferencedFullInfo": "Siemens.SimaticIT.MasterData.CHR_MS.MSModel.DataModel.CharacteristicSpecification",
      "Description": "Contains general information of a Quality Characteristic.\r\nQuality Characteristics allows you to verify the quality of your products. In details, they allows you:\r\n- Defining whether a produced material respects a specific characteristic or not (Attributive Characteristics). Example: you are inspecting a car and checking whether the paint is used to paint the car (the paint is available) or not.\r\n- Getting information on measurements and allowed tolerances, indicating whether a produced material respects a specific measurement, like length, weight, thickness (Variable Characteristics). Example: you are inspecting a car and checking that the paint thickness is the required one, according to defined tolerances.\r\n- Knowing whether visual defects (scuff marks, paint drops) have been detected in a produced material (Visual Characteristics). Example: you are inspecting a car and checking whether scuff marks are detected in the car paint.\r\n\r\nHow Quality Characteristics must be acquired at runtime is defined by the Inspection Definitions that are associated with Quality Characteristics.",
      "IsRevision": "True",
      "ArtifactType": "Entity",
      "Members": [
        {
          "Name": "Type",
          "Type": "Siemens.SimaticIT.MasterData.CHR_MS.MSModel.Types.CharacteristicType",
